        );
    }
    polygon_data.push_back(
        static_cast<int32_t>(-1 - (uniq_v_before + vertex_indices[v_offset+f.mIndices[pvi]]))
    );
}
```

The vulnerability is that `f.mIndices[pvi]` is used to index into `vertex_indices` at `v_offset + f.mIndices[pvi]`. If a face index `f.mIndices[pvi]` is >= `m->mNumVertices`, this causes an out-of-bounds read. This is a heap-buffer-overflow READ.

This is an FBX **exporter** vulnerability. The input is a 3D model file that gets imported (e.g., OBJ, PLY, etc.) and then exported to FBX. The crash happens during export when the imported mesh has faces with indices that exceed the vertex count.

